<details class="admin-details" id="catalog-glossary">
    <summary>How products and features fit together</summary>
    <ul class="admin-plain-list">
        <li><strong>Product</strong>: what an article is about (GitHub Copilot, Azure Functions). The names the AI returns link to a product by its name or an alias, so a name that includes a plan ('GitHub Copilot Business') can be an alias of the product. A product can belong to a parent product: GitHub Copilot CLI belongs to GitHub Copilot, so its articles and dates also show up on GitHub Copilot.</li>
        <li><strong>Feature</strong>: a capability of one product (Agent mode of GitHub Copilot). A date can be about a feature; a feature also has a description and a release date.</li>
        <li><strong>Date</strong>: an important date (preview, GA, retirement) that the AI found in an article, about a product and optionally a feature. Plans and editors are in its description.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="admin-result-summary">Features belong to a product and also apply to its child products.</p>
</details>
